From: UTDeck
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winewayland: fill the screen with a smaller game window (UTDECK_FILL)

Games without a render-scale option are played in a window smaller than the panel (borderless or
windowed 1200x540 on 2400x1080), as the phone's GPU cannot draw the full resolution; Lomiri shows
such a window as it is, in a corner, with its top panel. With UTDECK_FILL=1 the window is shown
over the whole screen, as gamescope does on the Steam Deck, while the game keeps seeing its own
window size:

- win32u (vulkan.c, window.c): a top-level window smaller than its monitor (not minimized or
  maximized) that creates a swapchain gets a host swapchain of the screen's size from patch 0006's
  scaler (fit by default, UTDECK_SCALE), its client surface is placed at the screen's origin, and
  the window is marked with two properties: the picture's rect and the screen's size.
- winewayland: when a marked window presents, it is made fullscreen, its own drawing is replaced
  by one black screen-sized buffer (so that input anywhere on the panel reaches it; there is no
  wp_viewporter on Lomiri to scale a buffer), and pointer and touch positions are mapped from the
  picture's rect back to its client area.
- The window is never resized by the compositor's configure (patch 0003 would follow a rotation
  and give the game a portrait window). Instead the driver records the configured fullscreen size
  (the screen in the phone's current orientation: 1080x2400 upright, 2400x1080 turned) in a third
  property; win32u then returns VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR once, the application recreates its swapchain,
  and the picture is fitted into that size (upright: a 1080x486 band for a 1200x540 game).

Launchers and dialogs create no swapchain and are not affected. Exclusive fullscreen games are
not either (they cover the monitor already).
